# sectop users and group (docs/architecture.md, Privilege split).
# install.sh installs this as /etc/sysusers.d/sectop.conf and adds one line:
#   m <admin user> sectop     (the UI reads /run/sectop, connects to the whois socket)
# sectop-feed: no members. The user helper's unit Group= and the collector's
# SupplementaryGroups=: the helper -> collector channel (/run/sectop-user/<user>/).
# sectop-home: the home watch (sectop-home@<user>.service), reads the desktop user's start
# places through ACL entries, writes /run/sectop-home/<user>/ for the collector.
# sectop-ids: the ids summary (sectop-ids.service), reads Suricata's eve.json through
# group suricata (unit SupplementaryGroups=, only when Suricata is installed), writes
# /run/sectop-ids/ for the collector.
g sectop      -
g sectop-feed -
u sectop      -:sectop  "sectop collector"  -  -
u sectop-net  -:sectop  "sectop net unit"   -  -
u sectop-home -:sectop-feed "sectop home watch" - -
u sectop-ids  -:sectop-feed "sectop ids summary" - -
